# Textrix server definitions — the only source of connections.
#
# Copy to ~/.textrix/.env (or .env in the folder TEXTRIX_HOME or --home
# names; or point TEXTRIX_ENV or --env at another path) and
# `chmod 600` it. Debug builds (`cargo run`) read `.textrix` in the repo
# root instead; it is git-ignored. Textrix will not start without it, and
# refuses to read secrets from it while other users can read the file.
#
# Every server defined here is connected on startup. Each one is a group of
# TEXTRIX_<NAME>_* keys; <NAME> is what `/connect <name>` and
# `/disconnect <name>` take (case-insensitive). Comment a server out to
# stop connecting to it.
#
#   HOMESERVER    Base URL or server name. Optional: discovered from the
#                 user ID's server via .well-known when omitted.
#   USER          Required. Full Matrix ID (@you:example.org) or localpart.
#   PASSWORD      Secret. Required for the first login on this machine;
#                 after that the saved session is reused. Keep it for
#                 /devices delete, which the server makes ask for it again.
#   RECOVERY_KEY  Secret, optional. Unlocks encrypted message history and
#                 verifies this device via cross-signing.
#   KEYS_PASSPHRASE
#                 Secret, optional. Encrypts the files /keys export writes
#                 and opens the ones /keys import reads (Element's format,
#                 so use the passphrase you gave Element for its files).
#
# Secrets are read only at the moment the Matrix API call needs them, handed
# straight to the SDK, and wiped from memory afterwards. They are never
# logged, shown in the UI, or typed into the client. A real environment
# variable with the same name overrides the file, so secrets can come from a
# password manager instead of living here:
#
#   op run --env-file ~/.textrix/.env -- textrix
#
# with values like  TEXTRIX_HOME_PASSWORD="op://Private/Matrix/password"

TEXTRIX_HOME_HOMESERVER=https://matrix.example.org
TEXTRIX_HOME_USER=@you:example.org
TEXTRIX_HOME_PASSWORD=
TEXTRIX_HOME_RECOVERY_KEY=
TEXTRIX_HOME_KEYS_PASSPHRASE=

# TEXTRIX_WORK_HOMESERVER=https://matrix.work.example
# TEXTRIX_WORK_USER=@you:work.example
# TEXTRIX_WORK_PASSWORD=
# TEXTRIX_WORK_RECOVERY_KEY=
